	abstract = {One promising approach to balance the need for fertilizer and the welfare of the environment, is the development of plants that can fix atmospheric nitrogen independently. This innovation would not only reduce the need for synthetic fertilizers and manure but also help mitigate climate change and the nitrogen crisis. To this end, we first need to better study the nitroplast, how it interacts with the host organism and how it could be potentially introduced into other cells.},
